## Adding a new command

1. Create `src/{{ pkg_name }}/commands/my_command.py`.
2. Define `register()` and a command function:

```python
import argparse

def register(subparsers) -> None:
    p = subparsers.add_parser("my-command", description="What it does.")
    p.add_argument("input", help="Required input.")
    p.add_argument("--flag", action="store_true", help="A boolean flag.")

def my_command(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:
    print(f"Running with: {args.input}, flag={args.flag}")
```

3. Import and wire it up in `src/{{ pkg_name }}/__main__.py`:

```python
from {{ pkg_name }}.commands.my_command import register as register_my, my_command
# In App.run():
register_my(subparsers)
# In the dispatch block:
elif args.command == "my-command":
    my_command(args)
```

